2) Bubble Sort :
class Solution {
    public int[] bubbleSort(int[] nums) {
         int n = nums.length;
         for(int i = 0 ; i < n-1 ;i++){
            boolean swapped = false;
            for(int j=0 ; j < n-1-i;j++){
               if(nums[j]>nums[j+1]){
                int temp = nums[j+1];
                nums[j+1]=nums[j];
                nums[j]=temp;
                swapped=true;
               }
            }
            if(!swapped){
                break;
            }
         }
        return nums;
    }
}
Time Complexity
Best Case: O(n) → Array is already sorted, so only one pass is needed.
Average Case: O(n²) → Multiple passes and comparisons are required.
Worst Case: O(n²) → Reverse sorted array; maximum comparisons and swaps.
Space Complexity
O(1) → Uses only a few extra variables (temp, swapped, i, j).

